course: dictionary
lesson: 7945
title: Reassure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To reassure someone means to make them feel less worried or afraid. The verb changes its form: reassures, reassured, reassuring. «A frightened child tells an adult, who checks and reassures her.» The adult checks that all is well, then tells the child, so the child feels calmer. That is what reassuring her means.
explain: Use the clues around the word. The child is frightened, and the adult does something helpful, so reassure must mean something like calm or comfort. Try your meaning in the sentence: «who checks and calms her» still makes sense, so your idea is right.
explain: Reassure often goes with someone and that: she reassured him that the dog was friendly. A reassuring smile is one that makes you feel safe. The noun reassurance means the comfort you feel, or the words or actions that give it.
fact: Reassure is a verb. Its noun is reassurance, and its adjective is reassuring.
fact: «Reassure» means to make someone feel less worried or afraid.
fact: «Reassuring» describes something that makes you feel calmer, as in «a reassuring smile».
fact: Common phrases are reassure someone that... and try to reassure someone.
fact: «Bezpechno» (Ukrainian) means it's safe, a word parents use to reassure a child.
exercise: «A frightened child tells an adult, who checks and reassures her.» What does reassures mean here? | Makes her more frightened | Takes her away from home | *Makes her feel less afraid | Ignores her completely
exercise: Which phrase means to make a friend feel less worried? | *Try to reassure | Try to shout | Try to forget | Try to frighten
exercise: Which is a reassuring thing to say to a nervous friend? | Be quiet and go away. | Nothing matters, so stop. | You should be scared. | *Don't worry, it will be okay.
test: Mum said, «You will be fine», to ___ me before the test. | *reassure | forget | hurt | scare
test: Which word is the noun for the comfort you feel when someone reassures you? | reassured | reassuring | reassure | *reassurance
exam: What does «a reassuring smile» show? | That the person is angry with you | That the person is very hungry | That the person is leaving the room | *That the person makes you feel safe and calm
